// fixture-236: MAN-DEP-OPTIONAL-FLAG-CLASH — non-optional LocalDep named same as declared flag
//
// spec/errors.md §MAN-DEP-OPTIONAL-FLAG-CLASH (NORMATIVE): a non-optional dep
// whose name collides with an already-declared flag MUST raise
// MAN-DEP-OPTIONAL-FLAG-CLASH.  The spec says "AN optional=#true dep's name
// collides with a declared flag, OR a non-optional dep shares a name with a
// declared flag" — NO restriction to dep form.  All five dep forms apply.
//
// This fixture uses a LocalDep (non-optional by definition — only UrlDep and
// NamedDep carry the optional field) named "mylib" which collides with the
// declared flag "mylib".
//
// Regression for R7-D1: Python _desugar_optional_deps (manifest.py) had an
// isinstance(dep, (UrlDep, NamedDep)) guard on the namespace-hygiene check,
// silently accepting a LocalDep/TarballDep/MemberDep that shares a flag name.
// Rust checks all five forms and raises MAN-DEP-OPTIONAL-FLAG-CLASH correctly.
// After fix: Python broadens the check to all dep forms; both impls raise.
name "myapp"
kind "application"
flags {
    mylib default=#false
}
deps {
    mylib local="../mylib"
}
